  "text": "proprium.dedicatio-sancti-michaelis-archangeli-epistola",
  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “Dedication of Saint Michael the Archangel” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "In those days, God signified those things which must shortly come to pass, sending through His Angel to His servant John; who bore witness to the word of God and to the testimony of Jesus Christ, to whatever he saw. Blessed is he who reads and hears the words of this prophecy, and keeps the things that are written in it; for the time is at hand. John to the seven churches that are in Asia: grace be to you and peace from Him who is and who was and who is coming, and from the seven spirits who are before His throne, and from Jesus Christ, who is the faithful witness, the firstborn of the dead, and the ruler of the kings of the earth, who has loved us and washed us from our sins in His own Blood.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w068", "w069"], "anchor": "w068", "gloss": "is coming" }] }
  },
